---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';

const lastUpdated = 'May 31, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title={`Terms of Use - ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="Terms of use for ghidini.net">
  <article class="prose-flux">
    <h1 class="mb-2 text-3xl font-bold">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="mb-8 text-sm text-(--color-muted-foreground)">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-(--color-muted-foreground)">
        By accessing and using ghidini.net, you accept and agree to be bound by these Terms of Use.
        If you do not agree to these terms, please do not use this website.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">2. Content</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-(--color-muted-foreground)">
        The content on this website is provided for informational purposes only. While I strive to
        keep the information accurate and up-to-date, I make no warranties about the completeness,
        reliability, or accuracy of any content. Any action you take based on the information on
        this website is at your own risk.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">3. Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-(--color-muted-foreground)">
        Unless otherwise stated, the content on this website (articles, code snippets, and guides)
        is the intellectual property of Alessandro Ghidini. Code snippets provided in blog posts are
        intended to be educational and may be used in your own projects unless explicitly noted
        otherwise.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">4. Code Examples</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-(--color-muted-foreground)">
        Code examples and snippets shared on this blog are provided "as is" without warranty of any
        kind. You are free to use them in your projects, but I am not responsible for any issues
        that may arise from their use. Always review and test code before using it in production
        environments.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">5. Comments and User Content</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-(--color-muted-foreground)">
        Blog posts and guides may include an optional comments section powered by
        <a
          href="https://giscus.app"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank"
          class="text-(--color-accent) hover:underline">giscus</a
        > and GitHub Discussions. The comments widget loads only after you explicitly choose to load it;
        doing so, and posting a comment, is entirely optional and independent of your acceptance of these
        Terms. How your data is handled is described in the
        <a href="/privacy" class="text-(--color-accent) hover:underline">privacy policy</a>. To post
        a comment you must sign in with a GitHub account and agree to GitHub&rsquo;s terms. You
        retain ownership of the content you post, but grant me the right to display it on this
        website.
      </p>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-(--color-muted-foreground)">
        You agree not to post content that is unlawful, defamatory, harassing, hateful, infringing,
        spam, or otherwise objectionable. I reserve the right to remove or moderate any comment at
        my sole discretion, and comments are also subject to GitHub&rsquo;s Acceptable Use Policies.
        Comments express the views of their authors, not mine.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">6. External Links</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-(--color-muted-foreground)">
        This website may contain links to external websites. I am not responsible for the content or
        privacy practices of these third-party sites. Following external links is at your own
        discretion.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">7. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-(--color-muted-foreground)">
        In no event shall I be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, special, or
        consequential damages arising from your use of this website or reliance on any information
        provided.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">8. Changes to Terms</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-(--color-muted-foreground)">
        I reserve the right to modify these terms at any time. Changes will be effective immediately
        upon posting to this page. Your continued use of the website after changes constitutes
        acceptance of the updated terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">9. Governing Law</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-(--color-muted-foreground)">
        These terms shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of Italy and the
        European Union, without regard to conflict of law provisions.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">10. Contact</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-(--color-muted-foreground)">
        If you have any questions about these Terms, please contact me at:
        <a href="mailto:info@ghidini.net" class="text-(--color-accent) hover:underline"
          >info@ghidini.net</a
        >
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
